# (build 105) The CRT page on the owner's ASUS ProArt P16, as tools/
# display_probe.c measured it (Arch Linux, Wayland, SDL 3.4.16): a 3840x2400
# OLED at a desktop scale of 1.9, HDR on with SDL's headroom 1.624 over an
# SDR white of 1.000. Windowed, high pixel density gives the window the
# panel's own pixels (960x672 points, 1824x1277 pixels): five display lines
# a scanline, so scanlines and the aperture grille, not yet the slot mask;
# fullscreen, ten, every mask. SDL's SDR white on Wayland is 1.0 with no
# nits said, so PEAK's AUTO takes it as BT.2408's 203 nits: 1.624 x 203 =
# 330 (before this build the page said 130, reading 1.0 as scRGB's 80).
# The words are the probe's PS2_DISPLAY lines. The route reads its own
# settings.json.
start new
wait screen title
display 1824x1277 full=3840x2400 hdr=1.624/1.000 sdr=203
press esc
press down
press down
press down
press down
press c
press c
expect crt scanlines ON
press down
press c
expect crt mask APERTURE GRILLE
expect crt summary GRILLE
press right
expect crt mask SLOT MASK / NEEDS FULLSCREEN
press down
press left
expect crt subpixels OTHER
press down
press right
expect crt hdr ON
press c
expect crt peak AUTO 330 NITS
expect crt white 200 NITS
wait ticks 5
shot p16_window_hdr
press b
wait ticks 16
shot p16_window_crt
display 3840x2400 fullscreen full=3840x2400 hdr=1.624/1.000 sdr=203
expect crt mask SLOT MASK
press up
press up
press right
expect crt mask SHADOW MASK
expect crt summary SHADOW MASK
wait ticks 14
shot p16_fullscreen_crt
press b
press b
expect escape-menu closed
